1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,780
There were forty gallons of clean water
in this gas station.

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:04,540
Finding them almost got you killed.

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,700
Day nineteen.

4
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:07,520
Your last bottle is empty.

5
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:11,130
But FEMA lists a hidden water source in
almost every building.

6
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:12,110
The water heater.

7
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,070
Forty gallons, in the back room.

8
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:15,370
You open the drain valve.

9
00:00:15,390 --> 00:00:16,270
Clean water.

10
00:00:16,290 --> 00:00:17,270
Weeks more.

11
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:20,270
But to reach it, you dragged the
shelves off the back door.

12
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:22,110
And you never put them back.

13
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:22,675
3 a.m.

14
00:00:22,695 --> 00:00:24,640
The back door clicks open.

15
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:25,940
One of them is inside.

16
00:00:25,960 --> 00:00:28,380
Between you and everything you own.

17
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:30,870
You run for the walk-in cooler and
hold the door shut.

18
00:00:30,920 --> 00:00:31,540
Dark.

19
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:32,300
Freezing.

20
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,760
Your breath turns to fog.

21
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:35,320
And it's scratching at the door.

22
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:38,940
On your belt: the cashier's handset, wired
to the speakers outside.

23
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,170
You see, they hunt by sound.

24
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:43,870
And the loudest thing for a mile
is pump four.

25
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,160
You press the button and bang
it on the wall.

26
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:46,860
It turns.

27
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,340
It follows the noise out the back
door, into the rain.

28
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,160
You slam the door and bury it under
every shelf you own.

29
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:53,930
You survived your mistake.

30
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:56,750
But you just told the whole
county where you are.

